INT. BOWLING CENTER, STATE FINALS - EVENING

Lanes polished to a shine. Overhead scoreboards. A banner reads "REGIONAL CHAMPIONSHIP." The pins crash in the distance.

COACH TERESA BIANCHI-ODEH (50s, windbreaker, clipboard) paces behind the team's lane. At the ball return, seniors CALEB STRUTHERS (18, broad) and PILAR NUÑEZ-WADE (17, wiry) wait their turns. Manager FELICITY OKONKWO (16, headset, stats binder) feeds numbers into a tablet. And at the end of the lane, anchor OSWALD "OZ" KETTERING (17, braces, shaking hands) rubs chalk on his fingers.

OVER THE PA (V.O.)
Final frame. Carson Valley leads by seven. Carson Valley, you have the lane.

BIANCHI-ODEH
Listen up. Oz, you need a strike. Just a strike. No spare helps us.

OZ
I know, Coach.

CALEB
He knows.

PILAR
Leave him alone.

PILAR
Oz. Breathe.

FELICITY
Percentage of strikes on the left oil pattern is--

BIANCHI-ODEH
Felicity, not now.

FELICITY
Sorry.

PILAR
Oz, you got this.

CALEB
Yeah, Oz, you got--

OZ
Please stop.

They stop. Oz takes the ball. Weighs it. Steps to the line. A quiet falls. He draws back, releases. The ball curves, rolls, rolls, hits. Nine pins fall. One wobbles, wobbles, wobbles.

CALEB
Come on.

PILAR
Fall, fall, fall.

FELICITY
Probability of the ten-pin falling is--

PILAR
Felicity.

FELICITY
Shutting up.

The ten-pin stands. Still. Dead still. Oz stares. His shoulders slump.

OZ
Sorry, Coach.

BIANCHI-ODEH
Don't be. Take the spare.

Oz takes the second ball. Walks to the line. The same quiet. He lets it go. It rolls straight down the right gutter's edge and clips the ten-pin from the side. It tumbles. Falls.

The scoreboard flashes. The team explodes. Caleb hoists Oz into the air. Pilar howls. Felicity types a number, then screams.

OVER THE PA (V.O.)
Final score. Brookfield Prep, two-eleven. Carson Valley, two-ten. Brookfield takes the title.

Everyone freezes. Slowly, one by one, they turn to Bianchi-Odeh, who is calmly capping her pen.

BIANCHI-ODEH
Pack up.
